[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n2_hugh"
text = "# DRAFT
# Prior Hugh on the north walk at dusk (night 2). If the merchant died, he wants to know why the guesthouse was left
# unlocked (n2_hugh_lock), and tells the porter the purse is gone (the merchant_purse note). He suspects the porter, and Walter.
# Otherwise he is merely cold, and has a word on the pardoner. If Thomas told the porter the prior walks at night,
# the porter can ask him why (n2_hugh_night): he turns it back on the porter.
== start
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> sent [if n1_merchant=prior]
-> cold

== dead
(The prior steps into your way on the walk, his wax tablet already open.)
-> dead_told [if reported_merchant=prior]
-> dead_none [if reported_merchant=none]
-> dead_ask

== dead_told
Hugh: You brought me the merchant this morning. The one thing you've done right.
-> dead_ask

== dead_none
Hugh: Your round goes past the fishpond, porter. You saw nothing? Nothing at all?
-> dead_ask

== dead_ask
Hugh: You turned down the merchant's bed. This morning he was in the fishpond. Was the guesthouse locked, porter?
* No. I didn't think to lock it. -> honest
* He was a guest, not a prisoner. -> guest
* What are you saying I did? -> accuse

== honest [set n2_hugh_lock=honest] [trust hugh 5]
Hugh: You didn't think. Anselm thought of it every night for thirty years.
-> purse

== guest [set n2_hugh_lock=guest]
Hugh: A prisoner would be alive this morning.
-> purse

== accuse [set n2_hugh_lock=accuse] [trust hugh -5]
Hugh: I'm not saying. I'm asking. You'll know when I start saying.
-> purse

== purse [note merchant_purse]
Hugh: He had a purse at your gate. You'll have seen it. There was none on him this morning.
Hugh: Thomas says he drowned drunk. Drunk men drown with their purses on.
-> purse_walter [if n1_walter=admitted]
-> ask

== purse_walter
Hugh: And you let the pardoner in after him. (He writes it on his tablet.) I'll be asking Walter about purses.
-> ask

== sent
(The prior watches you come down the walk.)
Hugh: You sent for me last night. (He looks almost surprised.) Good. That's the rule. Keep to it.
-> ask

== cold
(The prior watches you come down the walk, and doesn't move out of your way.)
Hugh: Porter. Your first night, and the house still standing. Don't let it go to your head.
-> walter_in [if n1_walter=admitted]
-> walter_out [if n1_walter=refused]
-> ask

== walter_in
Hugh: You let the pardoner in. Walter sells pigs' knuckles to widows and calls them saints. Next time, send for me.
-> ask

== walter_out
Hugh: You turned the pardoner away. Good. Anselm let him in whenever he knocked.
-> ask

== ask
* [if n2_thomas_prior] [if not n2_hugh_night] Why do you walk the abbey at night, Father Prior? -> night

== night [set n2_hugh_night] [trust hugh -5]
(His face doesn't change, but he closes his tablet.)
Hugh: Who told you that?
Hugh: I walk where I please in this house. I'm its prior. Where do you walk, porter, between Matins and Lauds?
-> end

== again
(He's writing on his tablet, and doesn't look up.)
Hugh: Supper, porter.
-> ask

== leave
Hugh: We're not done, porter.
"
